  "title": "Ship real type declarations for botframework-directlinespeech-sdk",
  "body": "> `botframework-directlinespeech-sdk` ships JavaScript as its type declarations.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed `botframework-directlinespeech-sdk` shipping JavaScript as type declarations, and the `createDirectLineSpeechAdapters` return type naming `webSpeechPonyfill` instead of `webSpeechPonyfillFactory`, in PR [#6037](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6037), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\ntsup emitted the bundled JavaScript as the package's `.d.mts`/`.d.ts`, and the `require` types pointed to a never-built `lib/index.d.ts`: TypeScript consumers got wrong types (ESM) or none (CommonJS). The package now ships hand-written declarations for both. The bundle's `createDirectLineSpeechAdapters` type returns `webSpeechPonyfillFactory`, as at runtime, not `webSpeechPonyfill`.\n\n## Design\n\n- Hand-written `index.d.ts` rather than converting to TypeScript (1,700 lines) or generating from JSDoc (there is none, so all `any`).\n- tsup emits it as `.d.mts` and `.d.ts`: one `src/index.d.ts` for both conditions makes ESM types \"masquerade as CJS\" (arethetypeswrong).\n- The bundle keeps its `as any`: `web-speech-cognitive-services`' `SpeechRecognition` is not assignable to `typeof SpeechRecognition`.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `directlinespeech/src/index.d.ts`: declarations for `createAdapters` and `buildInfo`; activities typed as interfaces are accepted\n- `directlinespeech/tsup.config.ts`: emits them\n- `directlinespeech/package.json`: `require` and top-level `types` point to `dist/*.d.ts`\n- `directlinespeech/test-d/`: tsd tests of the shipped declarations (options, result, `buildInfo`, invalid options), run by the \"Type definitions test\" job\n- `bundle/src/createDirectLineSpeechAdapters.ts`: `webSpeechPonyfillFactory` in the return type\n- `bundle/test-d/pass/create-direct-line-speech-adapters.test-d.ts`: checks it\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
